 - Hold-Select hotkey sheet: holding the gamepad hotkey button (default Select) alone for about 400 ms in a running, unpaused game shows the "Hold Select +" sheet over the stage with the current gamepad hotkeys (including Screen layout; rows that do not apply are greyed with the reason). Releasing it or pressing another button hides it; hotkeys fire as before.
 - Speed-up / fast-forward ([ADR 0018](adr/0018-player-speed-up.md)): Space or the header split button, speed 1.5× to 8× (default 2×, speed menu on the button), for cores that allow it; Emulation settings for speed, speed-up on start and audio; usable while the Session is shared.
 - Hotkeys (Controllers › Hotkeys): fullscreen (F11), diagnostics (F3), snapshot (F5), speed-up (Space), volume up/down (+ / −, repeat while held; up while muted unmutes), mute (M), screenshot (F12). Esc is fixed, always pauses and opens the Quick menu; F11 is the only key that leaves fullscreen. Gamepad hotkeys: hotkey button (default Select) plus a button, per action (fullscreen Select + B, speed-up Select + R2, volume Select + D-pad up/down, mute Select + X, screenshot Select + Y; tried with virtual joysticks only). Plugin hotkeys have no default, conflicts are shown, Uzume keys win.
-- Audio (0.19, stage 1): master volume 0-100 % (default 100) and mute, per PC, applied as a software gain to the local game and to watched Sessions; the Session share sent to viewers is unaffected. In game, the header "Sound" control (shows the volume, for example "5 %") opens the "Sound" popover (slider "My game", "Muted in the background", "Mute all" / "Unmute", "Sound settings"); hotkey changes show a short toast ("Volume 72 %", "Muted", "Sound on · 72 %"). Settings › This PC › Audio & video: Output (System default or a device, applies from the next game start), Mute when in the background (default on; watched Sessions stay audible), Volume steps 5 % / 10 % (default 5 %), Show volume on screen (default on). Audio stage 2 (0.23, [ADR 0033](adr/0033-together.md) D6): one mixer and one output sink for everything the app plays (the local game, watched tiles, voice, plugin sounds, soft-clipped); the Sound popover also has the sliders "Voice" (the voice channel, adjustable before voice chat exists) and "Plugin sounds"; in the Multiview the header button "Mixer" opens a popover with one slider per watched person (remembered per person on this PC) and "Mix all tiles" (off by default: only the one tile with the AUDIO tag is heard, as before; on: every tile and your game are mixed at their own levels and all carry the AUDIO tag). Plugins can play short sounds with `fb.sound` (permission `sound`). Video rows are not built yet.
